#: guis/GUI03_Fiber_Morphology_Statistics.py:2379
msgid "グループごとの統計値と群間比較の結果を、別のウィンドウに表示します。統計値と比較の保存もそのウィンドウで行います。開いたままヒストグラムを作成し直すと、内容が更新されます。"
msgstr ""
"Shows the statistics of each group and the between-group comparison in a "
"separate window. The statistics and the comparison are also saved from "
"that window. Creating the histogram again while it is open refreshes its "
"contents."

#: guis/GUI03_Fiber_Morphology_Statistics.py:2426
msgid "除外を適用"
msgstr "Apply exclusions"

#: guis/GUI03_Fiber_Morphology_Statistics.py:2432
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"バンドル横の {suffix} に記録された手動除外を適用します。Fiber Tracker "
"で除外したファイバーが集計から外れ、何本外れたかはログに出ます。OFF にすると、追跡された全てのファイバーを集計します。"
msgstr ""
"Apply the manual exclusions recorded in {suffix} beside the bundle. "
"Fibers excluded in the Fiber Tracker drop out of the aggregation, and the"
" log reports how many. Turn this off to aggregate every traced fiber."

#: guis/GUI03_Fiber_Morphology_Statistics.py:2439
msgid "連結を適用"
msgstr "Apply connection"

#: guis/GUI03_Fiber_Morphology_Statistics.py:2445
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"バンドル横の {suffix} に記録された連結結果を適用します。Fiber Tracker で連結して保存したバンドルは、そこで見ていたのと同じ"
" 1 "
"本のフィブリルとして集計されます。自動連結と手動連結は区別されません。記録されているのはどの断片が繋がっているかであり、探索はここでは実行されないため、集計対象は画面で確認したものと一致します。ファイルの無いバンドルは骨格断片のまま集計されるため、適用できた枚数はログに出ます。"
msgstr ""
"Apply the connection result recorded in the {suffix} file beside each "
"bundle. A bundle connected and saved in the Fiber Tracker is aggregated "
"as the same whole fibrils shown there. Automatic and manual connections "
"are not distinguished. What is recorded is which fragments are joined, "
"and no search runs here, so what is aggregated matches what you checked "
"on screen. A bundle with no file is aggregated as skeleton fragments, so "
"the log reports how many bundles the connection could be applied to."

#: guis/GUI03_Fiber_Morphology_Statistics.py:2461
msgid "計測量"
msgstr "Quantity"

#: guis/GUI03_Fiber_Morphology_Statistics.py:2470
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"比較する形態パラメータを選びます。{height} の {pixel} 集計以外はファイバー追跡の結果から算出します。{height} の "
"{pixel} "
"集計は骨格画素の高さをそのまま集めるため走査範囲が未記録のバンドルでも計測できますが、それ以外はバンドルに走査範囲が記録されている必要があります。"
msgstr ""
"Choose the morphological parameter to compare. Everything but {height} "
"per {pixel} is derived from fiber tracking. {height} per {pixel} collects"
" the heights of the skeleton pixels as they are, so it also works on a "
"bundle with no recorded scan size; everything else needs the bundle to "
"have one."

#: guis/GUI03_Fiber_Morphology_Statistics.py:2476
msgid "集計単位"
msgstr "Sample unit"

#: guis/GUI03_Fiber_Morphology_Statistics.py:2486
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"1 標本の数え方を選びます。{pixel} は骨格画素 1 点、{fiber} はファイバー 1 本（高さはファイバー内の中央値）、{image}"
" は画像 1 枚です。{image} "
"は含まれるファイバー値の中央値で、キンク密度は総キンク数を判定した長さの合計で割った値です。キンク密度は{image} でだけ集計します。1 "
"本ごとの密度は判定した長さ L に対して 0、1/L、2/L… の値しか取らず、分布の形が断片の長さで決まるためです。{pixel} "
"でまとめた分布は独立観測ではなく、長いファイバーほど重みが大きくなるため、群間比較では {fiber}・{image} "
"でも確認してください。{fiber} は同じ画像のファイバーを独立と数えるため、場所ごとの違いを踏まえて比べるときは {image} "
"を使います。{pixel} "
"はサンプリング間隔（nm/px）の小さい画像ほど標本が多くなるため、サンプリング間隔（nm/px）の異なる画像を同じグループに混ぜるとログに注意を出します。"
msgstr ""
"Choose what counts as one sample. {pixel} is one skeleton pixel, {fiber} "
"is one fiber (height uses the median within that fiber), and {image} is "
"one image. {image} takes the median of the fiber values it holds, and for"
" kink density the total kink count divided by the total judged length. "
"Kink density is aggregated per {image} only, because one fiber's density "
"takes only the values 0, 1/L, 2/L... of its judged length L, so the shape"
" of a per-fiber distribution is set by the fragment lengths. A "
"distribution pooled over {pixel} is not a set of independent observations"
" and weighs longer fibers more heavily, so also check {fiber} or {image} "
"when comparing groups. {fiber} counts the fibers of one image as "
"independent, so use {image} to compare with the difference between places"
" taken into account. {pixel} draws more samples from an image with a "
"finer pixel size, so the log warns when one group mixes images of "
"different pixel sizes."

#: guis/GUI03_Fiber_Morphology_Statistics.py:2503
msgid "図"
msgstr "Plot"

#: guis/GUI03_Fiber_Morphology_Statistics.py:2513
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{histogram} は 1 群の分布の形を示します。{ecdf} は累積分布を重ねて描くため、ビン幅に依存せずに群を比較できます。{box} "
"は各群の中央値と四分位数を並べて要約します。{ecdf} と {box} は常に重ね／並置表示になるため、縦並び・重ね表示の選択は使われません。"
msgstr ""
"{histogram} shows the shape of one group's distribution. {ecdf} overlays "
"the cumulative distributions, so groups can be compared without depending"
" on a bin width. {box} summarises each group's median and quartiles side "
"by side. {ecdf} and {box} always place every group on one axes, so the "
"stacked/overlaid choice is unused."

#: guis/GUI03_Fiber_Morphology_Statistics.py:2519
msgid "曲率窓"
msgstr "Curvature window"

#: guis/GUI03_Fiber_Morphology_Statistics.py:2533
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{curvature} "
"が回転角を測る弧長です。スケルトンの画素をそのままたどる線（{skeleton}、{pixels}）では一歩が直交か斜めに限られるため、窓が小さいと方向の量子化が値に表れます。大きくすると滑らかになりますが、窓より短いファイバーは測定対象から外れます。"
msgstr ""
"The arc length over which {curvature} measures its turning angle. On the "
"lines that follow the skeleton pixels as they are ({skeleton}, {pixels}),"
" every step is orthogonal or diagonal, so with a small window the "
"quantised direction shows in the value. A larger window smooths the "
"estimate but excludes every fiber shorter than it."

#: guis/GUI03_Fiber_Morphology_Statistics.py:2540
msgid "枠のファイバー"
msgstr "Fibers at frame"

#: guis/GUI03_Fiber_Morphology_Statistics.py:2551
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{length} だけに効く設定です。画像の枠に達したファイバーは走査範囲の外へ続いているため、長さが短く測られます。{include} "
"はそのまま集計し、枠に達した割合をグループごとに図とログに出します。{exclude} "
"は長さの集計から外します。ただし長いファイバーほど枠に達しやすいため、外すだけでは長いファイバーが過小になります。どちらの偏りも走査範囲で変わるため、比べるバンドルの走査範囲が違うとログで警告します。{ml}"
" は外したうえで、残った各ファイバーを枠内に収まる確率の逆数で重み付けし（Miles-Lantuejoul "
"補正）、その偏りを小さくします。走査範囲に近い長さは枠に収まる向きが少ないか無いため、差が残ります。交差で切れた断片は補正されず、その本数はログに出ます。{km}"
" は、枠と交差のどちらで切れた長さも扱います。自身の端を 2 つ持つファイバーを全長の観測、1 "
"つだけ持つファイバーを「計測した長さ以上」の観測として、ファイバーの長さの分布を推定します（Kaplan-Meier 推定）。{km} は "
"{fiber} "
"集計でだけ使えます。全長を見たうち最長のファイバーより長い側は推定できず、その割合は図とログに出ます。推定はグループごとに行います。そこに落ちる中央値や四分位数は、数値の代わりに「>"
" 全長を見た最長のファイバーの長さ」と書きます。ファイバーをリサンプリングした 95 % 区間はログと統計値の CSV "
"に出ます。平均・標準偏差・最頻値は空欄にします。{fiber} 集計の重み付きの標本には群間検定を行いません。{ml} の {image} "
"集計は、各画像の重み付き中央値を検定します。高さ・曲率・キンクは枠内の部分の測定として有効なため、この設定の影響を受けません。"
msgstr ""
"Applies to {length} only. A fiber that reaches the image frame continues "
"outside the scan, so its length is measured short. {include} aggregates "
"such fibers as they are, and the figure and the log report the share that"
" reach the frame, per group. {exclude} leaves them out of the length "
"statistics. A long fiber is more likely to reach the frame, however, so "
"leaving them out alone under-represents long fibers. Both biases depend "
"on the scan size, so the log warns when the compared bundles differ in "
"it. {ml} leaves them out and weights each remaining fiber by the inverse "
"of its chance of fitting inside the frame (the Miles-Lantuejoul "
"correction), which reduces that bias. A length approaching the scan size "
"fits inside the frame at few orientations or none, so a difference "
"remains there. Fragments cut at a crossing are not corrected; the log "
"reports how many there are. {km} handles lengths cut either at the frame "
"or at a crossing. It estimates the distribution of fiber lengths by "
"taking a fiber with two ends of its own as an observation of its whole "
"length, and one with only one end of its own as an observation that it is"
" at least as long as measured (the Kaplan-Meier estimate). {km} is "
"available for the {fiber} unit only. The part of the distribution beyond "
"the longest fiber seen whole cannot be estimated, and the figure and the "
"log report its share. The estimate is made per group. A median or "
"quartile that falls there is written, instead of a number, as \"> the "
"length of the longest fiber seen whole\". A 95 % interval from resampling"
" the fibers is given in the log and in the statistics CSV. The mean, "
"standard deviation and mode are left blank. Weighted samples at the "
"{fiber} unit are not tested between groups; at the {image} unit, {ml} "
"tests the weighted median of each image. Height, curvature and kinks "
"remain valid measurements of the part inside the frame, so this setting "
"does not affect them."

